  "body_markdown": "Skip to content\n\nCall or Text Us: (310) 954-9449\n\nRequest An Appointment\n\nPatient Registration\n\nHome\n\nAbout Us\n\nOur Team\n\nDr. Jonathan Shadi\n\nDr. Saman Vahedi\n\nOur Technology\n\nCone Beam 3D Imaging\n\nProcedures\n\nOral Surgery\n\nBone Grafting\n\nPre-Prosthetic Surgery\n\nPlatelet Rich Fibrin (PRF)\n\nOral Pathology\n\nOrthognathic (Corrective Jaw) Surgery\n\nDental Implants\n\nRestorative Dentistry\n\nFull Mouth Reconstruction\n\nImpacted Canines\n\nWisdom Teeth Removal\n\nEmergency Dentistry\n\nFacial Trauma Fractures\n\nSedation Dentistry\n\nPatient Center\n\nPatient Information\n\nInsurance & Finance\n\nAreas We Serve\n\nMar Vista\n\nPalms\n\nCulver City\n\nWestwood\n\nSawtelle\n\nCentury City\n\nBrentwood\n\nSanta Monica\n\nWest Los Angeles\n\nSurgical Instructions\n\nBefore Anesthesia\n\nOral Surgery Pre-Operative Instructions\n\nPost-Operative Instructions\n\nReferring Doctors\n\nBlogs\n\nContact Us\n\n\n# The Benefits of Corrective Jaw Surgery for Your Health and Appearance\n\n\nCorrective jaw surgery, also known as orthognathic surgery, is a transformative procedure that addresses various functional and aesthetic concerns caused by jaw misalignment. Whether the issue stems from genetics, trauma, or developmental abnormalities, orthognathic surgery can provide life-changing benefits for both your health and appearance. Here’s a closer look at the advantages of this procedure and how it can improve your quality of life.\n\n\n## Enhanced Jaw Function\n\n\nMisaligned jaws can lead to difficulties in chewing, speaking, and even breathing. Corrective jaw surgery realigns the upper and lower jaws to improve functionality, enabling smoother, pain-free movements. This can help you enjoy your favorite meals and communicate with confidence.\n\n\n### Relief from Jaw Pain and Disorders\n\n\nJaw misalignment often contributes to chronic conditions like temporomandibular joint (TMJ) disorders, which cause pain and discomfort in the jaw, neck, and shoulders. By correcting the jaw’s structure, orthognathic surgery can significantly reduce or eliminate these symptoms, restoring comfort and mobility.\n\n\n### Improved Breathing and Sleep Quality\n\n\nConditions like sleep apnea are frequently linked to structural jaw issues. Orthognathic surgery can open up the airway, improving breathing patterns and reducing the severity of sleep apnea. Better sleep quality translates to increased energy, improved focus, and enhanced overall health.\n\n\n### Enhanced Aesthetics\n\n\nCorrective jaw surgery can reshape your face, harmonizing your features and enhancing your overall appearance. It addresses concerns such as:\n\nA protruding or receding jaw\n\nFacial asymmetry\n\nAn open bite or crossbite\n\nThe improved facial structure often boosts self-esteem and confidence.\n\n\n### Long-Term Oral Health\n\n\nMisaligned jaws can place undue stress on your teeth, leading to uneven wear, gum disease, and tooth decay. By aligning the jaw correctly, orthognathic surgery promotes better oral hygiene and reduces the risk of long-term dental problems.\n\n\n### Speech Improvements\n\n\nJaw misalignment can impact speech clarity, making certain sounds difficult to pronounce. Post-surgery, many patients experience improved articulation and clarity, enhancing their ability to communicate effectively.\n\n\n### Who Is a Candidate for Corrective Jaw Surgery?\n\n\nOrthognathic surgery is often recommended for individuals with:\n\nSevere jaw misalignment that cannot be corrected with orthodontics alone\n\nChronic jaw pain or TMJ disorders\n\nDifficulty chewing, biting, or swallowing\n\nBreathing or sleep-related issues caused by jaw structure\n\nFacial asymmetry or disproportionate jaw growth\n\n\n### Transform Your Health and Appearance\n\n\nCorrective jaw surgery offers a life-changing solution for those struggling with jaw misalignment, enhancing both your health and appearance. At Wilshire Oral Surgery and Implant Center, our expert oral and maxillofacial surgeons are dedicated to providing personalized care, ensuring optimal results tailored to your unique needs. From initial consultation to post-surgery recovery, our team is here to guide you every step of the way.\n\nTake the first step toward better health, functionality, and confidence. Contact Wilshire Oral Surgery and Implant Center to schedule your consultation and learn how orthognathic surgery can transform your life. Visit our office in Los Angeles, California, or call (310) 954-9449 to book an appointment today.\n\n\n### Contact Information\n\n\n12300 Wilshire Blvd #326 Los Angeles, CA 90025\n\n(310) 954-9449\n\n\n### Hours of Operation\n\n\nMonday\n\n8:00am – 4:00pm\n\nTuesday\n\nWednesday\n\nThursday\n\nFriday\n\nSaturday\n\nClosed\n\nSunday\n\n© 2026 Wilshire Oral Surgery and Implant Center. All Rights Reserved.\n\nAccessibility Statement\n\nMEET US\n\nSurgical Instructio...\n\nBlog\n\nMeet Us\n\nPatient Registration Form\n\nPre-prosthetic Surgery\n\nOral Surgery Pre-operative Instructions\n\nIV Sedation / General Anesthesia\n\nPost-operative Instructions",
